WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.200
After an endless series of delays and reshoots,&nbsp;
Aquaman will get his second solo film just in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:10.440
time for Christmas. Before you dive in, here&nbsp;
is what you need to know before its premiere.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:15.480
"Aquaman and the Lost Kingdom" is slated for&nbsp;
release on December 22, 2023. Fans who have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:19.600
been following the DC Extended Universe will&nbsp;
know that "Lost Kingdom" suffered some drastic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:24.000
delays due to the shakeup that occurred following&nbsp;
the Warner Bros. Discovery merger. The movie was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:29.360
initially scheduled to be released on December&nbsp;
16, 2022, before being moved back to March 17,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:35.280
2023. The film was moved yet again to&nbsp;
December 25, 2023, and then to December 20.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:39.520
Finally, Warner Bros. decided to move&nbsp;
the film one more time to December 22,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:43.120
which is where it'll hopefully stay put.&nbsp;
December will be a big month for the studio,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:47.520
as they're releasing "Wonka," "Aquaman," and&nbsp;
"The Color Purple" back to back to back. Will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:51.760
their three-pronged play bring in the box office&nbsp;
dollars? The movies likely won't be competing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:56.000
for the same audiences, so if fans are in the&nbsp;
mood for superhero action during the holidays,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:59.920
"The Last Kingdom" might fare well&nbsp;
against its December competition.

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:05.000
As fans might recall, the first "Aquaman" saw our&nbsp;
hero defeat his half-brother, Orm, and take over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.800
as king of Atlantis. According to the official&nbsp;
synopsis, Aquaman's new reign comes under attack&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:14.640
after his old enemy, Black Manta, arrives in&nbsp;
Atlantis seeking revenge. This time though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:19.560
the villain has the power of the Black Trident&nbsp;
which unleashes a devastating and evil power.

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:22.840
Following the return of Black Manta,&nbsp;
Aquaman is forced to team up with his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:26.960
imprisoned brother as the two try desperately&nbsp;
to save their family's kingdom and the world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:30.400
from the destructive power of the Black&nbsp;
Trident. With these two brothers bickering,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:34.607
it's sure to be a blast as they battle all sorts&nbsp;
of aquatic enemies to protect their homeworld.

00:01:34.607 --> 00:01:36.720
"Good job, little brother. High five."

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:39.440
"Do not call me brother."

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:44.360
"Aquaman and the Lost Kingdom" stars Jason Momoa&nbsp;
as the Atlantean king, who also goes by the name&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:49.960
of Arthur Curry. Yahya Abdul-Mateen II and Patrick&nbsp;
Wilson reprise their roles from the first film as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:54.840
well, with Temeura Morrison and Nicole Kidman&nbsp;
also returning to play Tom Curry and Atlanna.

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:59.800
Also returning to the cast is Amber Heard, who&nbsp;
reprises her role as the Atlantean warrior Mera.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:04.440
Heard's involvement with the film continues to be&nbsp;
a source of heavy controversy among online fans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:08.800
with many still petitioning for her removal&nbsp;
from "Aquaman" after she lost a civil defamation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:13.760
verdict against Johnny Depp in 2022. Heard&nbsp;
is joined by action star Dolph Lundgren,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:17.520
who is set to appear in the film&nbsp;
as Mera's father, King Nereus.

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:22.200
When the original "Aquaman" swam into theaters&nbsp;
back in 2018, the undersea adventure earned a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:26.440
staggering $1.14 billion, which made&nbsp;
it the fifth highest-grossing movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:30.520
of the year. Needless to say, Warner Bros.&nbsp;
didn't want to screw around with success,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:35.400
so they brought on the same filmmaker who sailed&nbsp;
the original movie to box office glory: James Wan.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:40.120
In addition to helming both "Aquaman" movies, Wan&nbsp;
is no stranger to action fare, as he directed both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:45.360
"Furious 7" and "Death Sentence." Of course, most&nbsp;
moviegoers probably associate Wan with the horror&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:50.640
genre, as he also directed "Saw," "The Conjuring,"&nbsp;
and "Insidious," among other creepy films. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:55.680
evidently, he had his fair share of horror working&nbsp;
on "The Lost Kingdom," as Wan had to undergo three&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.680 --> 00:03:00.480
separate reshoots, which The Hollywood Reporter&nbsp;
described as "almost an unprecedented number."

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:04.760
Warner Bros. and DC have famously undergone&nbsp;
some regime changes over the last few years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:09.320
and evidently, new bosses demanded new angles on&nbsp;
the material. Despite all the behind-the-scenes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:13.400
drama, Wan got it done, and even though&nbsp;
multiple people have given him notes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:16.960
the filmmaker insists "The Lost&nbsp;
Kingdom" is still his creation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:21.320
telling Entertainment Weekly, "At the&nbsp;
end of the day, this is my movie."

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:24.800
In addition to bringing back Jason&nbsp;
Momoa and James Wan for the sequel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:28.640
the film also features the return of&nbsp;
screenwriter David Leslie Johnson-McGoldrick,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:32.720
a longtime collaborator of Wan's and the&nbsp;
writer behind the original "Aquaman" film.

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:35.440
"Are you invoking the Combat of the Kings?"&nbsp;

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:38.800
"Call it whatever you want.&nbsp;
I call it an ass whoopin'."

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:42.840
Aside from "Lost Kingdom," Johnson-McGoldrick&nbsp;
has also written screenplays for films like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:47.480
"Wrath of the Titans," and "The Conjuring 2" and&nbsp;
television shows like "The Walking Dead." Early&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:51.200
reports indicated that at least some of the&nbsp;
story for "Lost Kingdom" was based on a pitch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:55.680
that Momoa himself created after the filming of&nbsp;
the first "Aquaman." However, as of right now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.680 --> 00:04:00.080
it's unclear how much of that pitch made&nbsp;
it into Johnson-McGoldrick's final script.

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:04.160
While there have been a few exceptions here and&nbsp;
there, such as the R-rated "Zack Snyder's Justice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:10.160
League," most DCEU movies come ready to rock with&nbsp;
a PG-13 rating. After all, it's the sweet spot for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:15.080
blockbuster success. It's just edgy enough so you&nbsp;
know there's some violence and mild cursing, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:20.280
it's tame enough so kids and teens can watch. All&nbsp;
the highest-grossing movies are PG-13, and that's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:25.080
also true for DC titles such as "Wonder Woman,"&nbsp;
"Man of Steel," and the original "Aquaman."

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:27.840
So it should come as no surprise&nbsp;
that "Aquaman and the Lost Kingdom"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:32.560
will be rated PG-13. The aquatic adventure&nbsp;
earned that rating due to "sci-fi violence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:36.960
and some language." Expect the same sort of&nbsp;
content you saw in the first "Aquaman" film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:41.440
and chances are good that you won't be&nbsp;
shocked by anything you see on the screen.

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:45.320
After the film's title announcement earlier&nbsp;
that month, production for "Aquaman and the Lost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:51.120
Kingdom" began in late June 2021. While the first&nbsp;
film was shot in Australia, Italy, and Morocco,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:55.160
"The Lost Kingdom" began production in the&nbsp;
United Kingdom where most of the film was shot.

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:59.160
With so much of "Aquaman and the Lost Kingdom"&nbsp;
taking place underwater, it makes sense that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:03.760
picture would be shot at Warner Bros. Studios in&nbsp;
London, something that fans taking the studio tour&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:08.600
confirmed back in July 2022. Though principal&nbsp;
photography had wrapped six months earlier,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:12.680
additional reshoots with Ben Affleck's&nbsp;
Batman took place in the summer of 2022.

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:16.480
Beyond Europe, "The Lost Kingdom" spent some&nbsp;
time in the United States. Throughout the back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:21.480
half of 2021, Los Angeles and Hawaiian units&nbsp;
shot additional material, with lead stars Jason&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:27.000
Momoa and Patrick Wilson seen on set in Malibu&nbsp;
on the very last day of principal photography.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:31.080
Most comic book and superhero movies are&nbsp;
generally inspired by the source material, so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:35.480
it shouldn't come as a surprise that "Aquaman and&nbsp;
the Lost Kingdom" draws from those same sources.

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:39.200
At the end of the trailer for the movie,&nbsp;
Warner Bros. and DC Comics promoted a few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:43.080
graphic novels that showcase the recent&nbsp;
history of our favorite Atlantian king.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:47.720
"The Trench" and "War for the Throne" are both&nbsp;
stories written by DC scribe Geoff Johns when he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:52.040
reinvented Aquaman for a modern audience. The&nbsp;
third book, "The Drowning," was helmed by Dan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:56.240
Abnett and set during the "DC Rebirth" era,&nbsp;
which sought to combine the traditional DC&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.240 --> 00:06:00.640
status quo with modern stories in a blended&nbsp;
universe. "The Drowning" is also notable due&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:04.840
to Arthur's attempts to make peace between&nbsp;
his undersea people and the surface world.

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:09.080
Of course, these aren't the only Aquaman stories&nbsp;
that likely inspired "The Lost Kingdom," but given&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:13.800
that they're being officially promoted by the&nbsp;
film, there's probably a strong correlation.

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:17.520
It's no secret that the DC Extended&nbsp;
Universe timeline is a bit of a mess.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:21.160
Despite starting strong with a clear vision&nbsp;
for a more mature take on the franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:24.880
everything after "Justice League" feels&nbsp;
pretty disjointed. Not even Zack Snyder's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:28.920
long-anticipated director's cut of "Justice&nbsp;
League" could fix the DCEU, leaving its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:34.160
fate up in the air until James Gunn and Peter&nbsp;
Safran took over in 2023 and axed it for good.

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:38.360
Following "Man of Steel" was "Batman&nbsp;
v Superman: Dawn of Justice" in 2016,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:41.640
which marked the first tease of Jason&nbsp;
Momoa's Aquaman, and the following year&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:46.120
brought "Justice League." After that, the&nbsp;
Atlantian got his own feature film in 2018,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:49.640
which is set about a year after Steppenwolf&nbsp;
attacked Earth and the Justice League was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:54.080
formed. In the years following, the DCEU&nbsp;
opted to highlight characters such as Shazam,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:58.280
Harley Quinn, and Peacemaker in a variety&nbsp;
of projects leading into the 2020s.

00:06:58.280 --> 00:07:03.120
Taking place around the events of 2022's&nbsp;
"Black Adam" and 2023’s "Shazam! Fury of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:07.240
the Gods," and possibly after "The Flash,"&nbsp;
the "Aquaman" sequel continues Arthur's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.240 --> 00:07:11.960
story as the DCEU closes shop. Where "Blue&nbsp;
Beetle" fits into all this, we don't know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.960 --> 00:07:16.720
but we know that "The Lost Kingdom"&nbsp;
marks the official end of the DCEU.

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:21.040
After his brief "found footage" cameo in&nbsp;
"Batman v Superman: Dawn of Justice," Jason&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:26.000
Momoa made his first official appearance in 2017's&nbsp;
"Justice League." When Batman first meets him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:30.000
Arthur is disillusioned and depressed,&nbsp;
having been cast out by his own people.

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:33.440
"Strong man is strongest&nbsp;
alone. You ever heard that?"&nbsp;

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:35.840
"That's not a saying. That's the opposite of what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:37.600
the saying is."
"Yup."

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:40.240
It's only after meeting others&nbsp;
like him and saving the world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.240 --> 00:07:42.920
that he sees the value in being a hero and a king.

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:46.320
A year later, Arthur is confronted by&nbsp;
Mera and Vulko, who need his help to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:50.160
save Atlantis. Arthur's half-brother Orm&nbsp;
is quickly running the kingdom into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:53.760
ground and aims to declare war on the&nbsp;
surface world. This leads to Arthur and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:58.240
Mera discovering the Trident of Atlan, finding&nbsp;
his mother Atlanna, and reclaiming the throne&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:02.800
after defeating Orm. "Aquaman" ends with&nbsp;
Arthur now ruling as the king of Atlantis.

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:07.680
Unfortunately, Aquaman doesn't appear much in the&nbsp;
DCEU after that. He's mentioned here or there in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:12.720
movies like "Shazam!," but it wasn't until a cameo&nbsp;
in the Season 1 finale of "Peacemaker" that Momoa&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:17.280
returned to the role, alongside Ezra Miller's&nbsp;
Flash. Speaking of, Arthur drunkenly reunites&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:21.960
with Barry Allen at the end of "The Flash" too,&nbsp;
which is fitting given how that movie wraps up.

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:26.120
Before James Gunn and Peter Safran opted&nbsp;
against saving the DCEU, the franchise was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.120 --> 00:08:30.480
going in a very different direction. Following&nbsp;
his turn in "The Flash," Michael Keaton's Batman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:34.880
was set to appear in "Aquaman 2," as well&nbsp;
as in the now-scrapped "Batgirl" movie.

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:38.360
But other plans were made. There was a&nbsp;
time when "Aquaman and the Lost Kingdom"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:41.400
was meant to premiere before the events&nbsp;
of "The Flash," and because of that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.400 --> 00:08:45.880
reshoots were made to replace Keaton's cameo with&nbsp;
Ben Affleck's version of the character. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:50.640
fans were excited by the news, and many had hope&nbsp;
that the DCEU was about to find its footing again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:53.560
especially after Henry Cavill's&nbsp;
way-too-brief return as Superman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:56.920
at the end of "Black Adam." And&nbsp;
then Gunn and Safran came in.

00:08:56.920 --> 00:09:03.040
DC Films became DC Studios, and the DCEU was&nbsp;
retconned in favor of the upcoming DC Universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:07.520
which aims to reboot the live-action franchise&nbsp;
anew with a brand new Batman and Superman.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:12.920
Needless to say, Batman's cameo — be it&nbsp;
Affleck or Keaton — is deep underwater.

00:09:12.920 --> 00:09:15.640
In the first "Aquaman," we learn&nbsp;
all about young Arthur's journey&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:19.200
to becoming the man who eventually helps&nbsp;
save the world and unite the kingdoms of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:23.880
Atlantis. Invaluable in his formation from a&nbsp;
troubled youth to kingly material is Vulko,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:27.320
who watches out for Arthur throughout&nbsp;
his whole life. Vulko makes his first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.320 --> 00:09:31.400
official DCEU appearance in "Aquaman,"&nbsp;
where he helps Arthur take the throne.

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:36.160
Fans may be disappointed to learn that Willem&nbsp;
Dafoe won't be returning as Vulko in "Aquaman 2,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:40.240
though it's not because he's off playing the Green&nbsp;
Goblin for Marvel again. According to director&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:45.680
James Wan, Vulko's absence is due to a scheduling&nbsp;
conflict. Wan revealed to Entertainment Weekly,

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:49.720
"Part of the reason was because [Dafoe's] schedule&nbsp;
did not work out for us, but what that allowed me&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.720 --> 00:09:54.720
to do was expand on Atlanna's role. Atlanna in&nbsp;
this one ultimately becomes Arthur's advisor."

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:59.160
Traditionally, Vulko serves as Aquaman's&nbsp;
faithful advisor in the world of DC Comics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:03.120
but here on the screen, it seems that Nichole&nbsp;
Kidman's Atlanna will fill that role instead.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:06.240
It's fitting, though, and allows Arthur&nbsp;
and his mother the much-needed face time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:11.280
that they've been deprived of for so long.&nbsp;
Still, it's sad we won't see Dafoe return.

00:10:11.280 --> 00:10:15.880
In the first "Aquaman," it's revealed that there&nbsp;
are seven kingdoms of Atlantis. As its king,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:19.240
Arthur's quest to unite them is&nbsp;
near the top of his to-do list,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.240 --> 00:10:22.720
but we're a bit fuzzy on what the&nbsp;
seventh kingdom might actually be.

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:26.040
"The Lost Nation had not yet vanished. Together,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.040 --> 00:10:28.680
they were the greatest empire&nbsp;
the world had ever seen."

00:10:28.680 --> 00:10:31.880
Of course, there's Atlantis itself,&nbsp;
and we soon learn of the others,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.880 --> 00:10:34.240
which include Xebel, the Kingdom of the Fishermen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:38.680
the Kingdom of the Brine, the Kingdom of&nbsp;
the Deserters, and the monstrous Trench.

00:10:38.680 --> 00:10:43.120
Though Atlantis, Xebel, the Trench, and the&nbsp;
Deserters were all addressed in the DC continuity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:47.640
before the 2018 film, the comic book versions of&nbsp;
the final three kingdoms weren't revealed until&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:52.400
afterward in the "Echoes of A Life Lived Well"&nbsp;
arc. The Brine is the first, being transplanted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.400 --> 00:10:56.760
into the comics from the DCEU, and the Kingdom&nbsp;
of the Wrights and the Kingdom of the Sea Lights&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.760 --> 00:11:00.760
followed. The Wrights are a bunch of underwater&nbsp;
rodents, while the Sea Lights are strange&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:06.240
bioluminescent humanoids. More than likely, the&nbsp;
film will take a completely different approach.

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:10.400
In the trailer for "Aquaman and the Lost Kingdom,"&nbsp;
Arthur and Mera are married, and they have a son&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:14.560
of their own. This begs the question if what&nbsp;
we see in "The Lost Kingdom" is in line with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.560 --> 00:11:18.920
what happens in the comics. Like anything that&nbsp;
deals with Aquaman's comic book history, it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.920 --> 00:11:25.440
somewhat complicated, but there are clear answers.&nbsp;
In 1965, "Aquaman #23" hit stores, and "Aquababy"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.440 --> 00:11:31.200
was born. That was the actual nickname for Arthur&nbsp;
Curry, Jr., the firstborn son of Aquaman and Mera.

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:37.160
Unfortunately, the happy family didn't stay happy&nbsp;
forever. In "Adventure Comics #452," Aquaman and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.160 --> 00:11:42.200
Aqualad are forced into a battle to the death&nbsp;
by Black Manta, who uses young Arthur Jr. as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:47.840
leverage. As expected, Aquaman defeats Manta, but&nbsp;
at a terrible price. His son is ultimately killed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.840 --> 00:11:52.080
by the supervillain, suffocating as a result&nbsp;
of his captivity. This drove a wedge between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:57.040
Aquaman and Mera for decades. Eventually, though,&nbsp;
they're able to rekindle and save their marriage.

00:11:57.040 --> 00:12:01.080
Aquaman has other children too. Aqualad,&nbsp;
later known as Tempest was considered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:05.040
Aquaman and Mera's adopted son, while&nbsp;
A.J. was their second child together&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:09.400
years later. Arthur also had a child named&nbsp;
Koryak with an Inuit woman at some point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.400 --> 00:12:15.160
and in the current DC Rebirth continuity, Aquaman&nbsp;
and Mera only have a daughter named Andrina.

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:19.720
Also appearing in the trailer for "Aquaman and the&nbsp;
Lost Kingdom" is Black Manta, who swore vengeance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:24.400
on Aquaman back in the first movie after the&nbsp;
superhero refused to save his dying father. Of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:24.400 --> 00:12:28.560
course, the comic book version of their rivalry&nbsp;
is much darker than that, with Aquaman purposely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:33.280
killing Manta's father in revenge following his&nbsp;
own father's death. Additionally, recent comics&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:37.560
have revealed that Manta is actually a long-lost&nbsp;
descendant of the Kingdom of the Deserters.

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:41.360
In the DCEU, however, Manta seems to&nbsp;
be completely human, which puts him at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:45.800
a significant disadvantage when facing off&nbsp;
against a superhero like Aquaman. Therefore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:45.800 --> 00:12:50.680
using Atlantean technology gifted to him by&nbsp;
Ocean Master, Manta has sworn revenge on his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:50.680 --> 00:12:54.720
adversary. But this time around, Black Manta's&nbsp;
abilities have been upgraded through the use of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.720 --> 00:12:59.200
the previously unseen Black Trident. This&nbsp;
magical artifact originates from the time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:03.520
of the first King Atlan and seems to give&nbsp;
the one who wields it incredible powers.

00:13:03.520 --> 00:13:07.040
Though it's unlikely a direct adaptation&nbsp;
of either, this new Black Trident seems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:07.040 --> 00:13:10.440
to borrow from two different weapons&nbsp;
from Aquaman's comic book adventures:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:10.440 --> 00:13:15.040
the Trident of Triton and the Dead King's&nbsp;
Scepter. Triton's trident simply directed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:19.440
the Olympian's power, while the Dead King's&nbsp;
Scepter gave the user control of the sea.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:24.146
From what we see of the Black Trident in&nbsp;
the trailer, it may even unleash the dead.

00:13:24.160 --> 00:13:26.920
Despite being mentioned elsewhere&nbsp;
in the "Aquaman 2" trailer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:26.920 --> 00:13:30.880
Mera only appears once in the entire thing,&nbsp;
with a brief glimpse at her as she attempts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:30.880 --> 00:13:34.880
to break into some sort of underwater craft.&nbsp;
While it might be easy to immediately blame&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:34.880 --> 00:13:38.440
her lack of screen time in the trailer,&nbsp;
and possibly the finished film as well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:38.440 --> 00:13:42.880
on the recent and very public defamation trial&nbsp;
between Amber Heard and her ex-husband Johnny&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:48.360
Depp, that might not be the full story. Warner&nbsp;
Bros. executive Walter Hamada said in 2022,

00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:52.520
"[Jason Momoa and Amber Heard] didn't really&nbsp;
have a lot of chemistry together. The reality is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:52.520 --> 00:13:55.680
it's not uncommon on movies for&nbsp;
two leads to not have chemistry."

00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:58.080
"Your majesty, there is no victory in defeating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:58.080 --> 00:14:02.320
the ignorant. Your brother&nbsp;
is clearly an imbecile."

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:06.320
Hamada added that a lot of their "chemistry"&nbsp;
was developed off-set during post-production,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:10.240
making us wonder how much Mera will appear in&nbsp;
"The Lost Kingdom" at all. But, according to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:15.040
director James Wan, this was always the plan for&nbsp;
the sequel. He explained to Entertainment Weekly,

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:18.920
"I always pitched this to everyone from the&nbsp;
get-go. The first 'Aquaman' was Arthur and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:23.360
Mera's journey. The second movie was always&nbsp;
going to be Arthur and Orm. So, the first was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:23.360 --> 00:14:28.440
a romance action-adventure movie, the second&nbsp;
one is a bromance action-adventure movie."

00:14:28.440 --> 00:14:32.440
A modern master of horror, Wan rose to&nbsp;
international acclaim when he co-created&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:32.440 --> 00:14:37.160
and directed the first "Saw" back in 2004.&nbsp;
The film was so popular that a sequel was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:37.160 --> 00:14:42.080
greenlit every year for the next six years&nbsp;
until "Saw 3D" in 2010. But even then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:42.080 --> 00:14:44.720
Wan's time with the genre had only just begun.

00:14:44.720 --> 00:14:49.200
In 2010, Wan directed the first "Insidious,"&nbsp;
which starred future "Aquaman" actor Patrick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:53.680
Wilson and spawned a plethora of&nbsp;
sequels. A few years later in 2013,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:53.680 --> 00:14:58.280
Wan directed "The Conjuring," which likewise&nbsp;
sparked an entire cinematic universe. Since then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:58.280 --> 00:15:02.920
he's worked on several other horror movies,&nbsp;
including 2021's "Malignant." No wonder Wan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:02.920 --> 00:15:06.880
used his trademark horror techniques during&nbsp;
the Trench sequence in the first "Aquaman."

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:11.200
So when the trailer for "The Lost Kingdom"&nbsp;
shows an undead army controlled by Black Manta,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:11.200 --> 00:15:13.120
it's no wonder Wan admitted to adding a certain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:13.120 --> 00:15:17.680
horror flare back into the sequel.&nbsp;
He said at 2020's DC Fandome event,

00:15:17.680 --> 00:15:21.440
"Just like the first movie had a touch of my&nbsp;
horror sensibility, you know, in regards to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:25.800
the Trench sequence, I would say there will&nbsp;
be a little bit of that in this next one."

00:15:25.800 --> 00:15:29.960
Following the release of the first "Aquaman"&nbsp;
in 2018, James Wan announced the development&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:29.960 --> 00:15:34.760
of a horror-infused spin-off centered around the&nbsp;
Trench. These sea-dwelling beasts first appeared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:34.760 --> 00:15:39.440
in Geoff Johns' "Aquaman" run during the "New 52"&nbsp;
rebrand, and they've since risen to popularity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:39.440 --> 00:15:44.280
after appearing in the first film. Producer&nbsp;
Peter Safran told The Hollywood Reporter in 2019,

00:15:44.280 --> 00:15:48.840
"We always, even from the early concept art&nbsp;
days, loved the idea of a 'Trench' movie."

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:52.040
He revealed that "The Trench" was meant&nbsp;
to arrive in theaters before "Aquaman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:52.040 --> 00:15:56.600
and the Lost Kingdom." But only two years later,&nbsp;
Walter Hamada shook things up with the DC brand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:56.600 --> 00:16:01.160
axing the project. While that was disappointing&nbsp;
news in and of itself, fans became even more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:01.160 --> 00:16:05.640
disillusioned after Wan commented further that&nbsp;
October. While showcasing Black Manta's new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:05.640 --> 00:16:09.920
look for "The Lost Kingdom," on Instagram&nbsp;
James Wan revealed something interesting,

00:16:09.920 --> 00:16:12.920
"I'll let you in on a secret, the&nbsp;
canceled Trench spin-off movie was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:15.720
really going to be a secret Black Manta movie."

00:16:15.720 --> 00:16:19.040
No doubt, fans of the DC supervillain&nbsp;
were floored by this news,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:22.080
which only proves that Wan had even&nbsp;
bigger plans for the character and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:26.720
the greater Aqua-verse. It's too bad the&nbsp;
same couldn't be said about Warner Bros.

00:16:26.720 --> 00:16:31.440
With the news that both Batman and Superman would&nbsp;
be recast for the DC Universe reboot and reports&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:31.440 --> 00:16:34.880
that Gal Gadot likely isn't returning as&nbsp;
Wonder Woman, it's understandable that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:34.880 --> 00:16:39.160
fans would wonder about the fate of Jason&nbsp;
Momoa's Aquaman. With DC's biggest hitters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:43.600
being tossed to the wayside in favor of new,&nbsp;
updated models, chances are that the beloved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:47.600
King of Atlantis will be next. "The Flash" may&nbsp;
have kept Ezra Miller's Barry Allen and Jason&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:47.600 --> 00:16:52.520
Momoa's Arthur Curry around for now, but things&nbsp;
could quickly change. At least in Momoa's eyes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:52.520 --> 00:16:57.560
there won't be another Aquaman in the near future.&nbsp;
Speaking with Variety in 2023, following the news&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:57.560 --> 00:17:01.560
of James Gunn and Peter Safran's intention&nbsp;
to reboot the movie universe, he said,

00:17:01.560 --> 00:17:06.280
"I'll always be Aquaman. Ain't anyone coming&nbsp;
in there and taking s---. There might be some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:06.280 --> 00:17:11.200
other characters, too. I can play other things,&nbsp;
too. I can be funny and savage and charming."

00:17:11.200 --> 00:17:13.280
With rumors swirling that Momoa is slated to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:13.280 --> 00:17:17.560
appear as Lobo in some point in the&nbsp;
near future, Peter Safran told io9,

00:17:17.560 --> 00:17:22.680
"Jason always thought Aquaman was a trilogy, in&nbsp;
his own mind, but he also loves Lobo. He's been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:26.800
very clear about that, too. He's never&nbsp;
going to play two characters, but..."

00:17:26.800 --> 00:17:31.360
James Gunn then interrupted Safran, saying,&nbsp;
"We'll figure it out after 'Aquaman 2.'" For&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:35.320
now, we'll just have to wait and see&nbsp;
what will become of Momoa's Aquaman.

00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:39.280
One of the biggest questions on fans' minds&nbsp;
concerning "Aquaman and the Lost Kingdom"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:39.280 --> 00:17:42.400
is whether it will get a follow-up of&nbsp;
its own. More than likely, that will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:42.400 --> 00:17:45.360
depend on how well the blockbuster&nbsp;
does in theaters this Christmas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:45.360 --> 00:17:51.360
but that may not be the only competing factor.&nbsp;
In September of 2023, James Wan told Screen Rant,

00:17:51.360 --> 00:17:54.000
"I'm aware of [the impending DCU reboot]. I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:57.640
I use the analogy that I'm living in a house&nbsp;
that's getting renovated, but the beauty about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:57.640 --> 00:18:01.720
Aquaman is that we've always designed these&nbsp;
two films to be within their own world."

00:18:01.720 --> 00:18:05.840
Given Wan's confidence, it's possible that future&nbsp;
installments could go the way of Matt Reeves'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:05.840 --> 00:18:10.600
out-of-continuity project "The Batman." It could&nbsp;
be a viable way to keep Momoa around. But that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:10.600 --> 00:18:15.160
doesn't mean the horror-turned-superhero director&nbsp;
wants to go a third round in the ring. When asked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:15.160 --> 00:18:19.120
by Entertainment Weekly if he'd be interested&nbsp;
in doing a third "Aquaman" film, he said,

00:18:19.120 --> 00:18:23.080
"Oh, buddy. I don't know. This film&nbsp;
has taken up so, so much of my life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:27.280
so much of my time, all I can think&nbsp;
about now is taking a long break."

00:18:27.280 --> 00:18:31.120
One can hardly blame him. Production was&nbsp;
stalled because of the COVID-19 pandemic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:31.120 --> 00:18:33.920
his Black Manta-centered spin-off&nbsp;
"The Trench" was canceled,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:33.920 --> 00:18:38.600
and the entire DCEU went up in flames. It's&nbsp;
entirely possible that this could be the end&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:38.600 --> 00:18:42.920
of Aquaman's on-screen adventures,&nbsp;
though we certainly hope for more.

00:18:42.920 --> 00:18:46.520
While James Wan might see his "Aquaman"&nbsp;
movies as their own thing apart from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:46.520 --> 00:18:51.680
greater DCEU or DCU, it's clear that Warner&nbsp;
Bros. and the folks at DC Studios don't see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:51.680 --> 00:18:55.920
it the same way. When asked about&nbsp;
the four DC-related movies of 2023,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:55.920 --> 00:18:59.880
James Gunn explained how they'll fit&nbsp;
into his larger plans, revealing to io9,

00:18:59.880 --> 00:19:03.760
"I think that we've gotten lucky with the next&nbsp;
four movies. We have 'Shazam,' which leads into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:03.760 --> 00:19:08.560
'Flash,' which resets everything, which then goes&nbsp;
into 'Blue Beetle,' which is totally disconnected,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:08.560 --> 00:19:13.040
[and that] goes into 'Aquaman,' which leads&nbsp;
into 'Superman,' our first big project."

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:16.960
How exactly "Aquaman and the Lost Kingdom"&nbsp;
connects to a movie like "Superman: Legacy" is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:21.480
currently unknown. The Gunn-helmed reboot is meant&nbsp;
to propel the Man of Steel into a new universe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:21.480 --> 00:19:26.000
that also includes heroes such as Hawkgirl and&nbsp;
the Guy Gardner Green Lantern. If there were to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:30.480
be another sequel, it's possible that it could&nbsp;
fit into Gunn's newly minted DCU, especially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:34.600
if he wants this interpretation of Aquaman to&nbsp;
be a building block for his larger universe.

00:19:34.600 --> 00:19:38.960
Of course, given how popular multiverses&nbsp;
are nowadays, there's always that avenue,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:38.960 --> 00:19:42.800
though it seems that Gunn wants to stay&nbsp;
away from other worlds for now. "Superman:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:42.800 --> 00:19:46.440
Legacy" will follow a younger&nbsp;
Superman in an even younger universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:46.440 --> 00:19:49.639
which makes one wonder how an&nbsp;
experienced Aquaman might fit in.

